us/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-10T20:06:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-10T20:06:14Z","body":"> Documentation is entirely fine now. Now it's worth questioning if reusing the enum like this is reasonable.\r\n\r\nIf it's not - I wash my hands and let @tetrapod00 continue to develop it on its own.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466891811/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466899191","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99033#issuecomment-2466899191","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99033","id":2466899191,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TCeT3","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-10T20:14:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-10T20:17:19Z","body":"I haven't looked closely at this code yet, and it's been a month or so since I did any visual shader work. Some of the visual shader nodes have very similar, but not shared, enums for the types they operate on (like `scalar`, `vec2`, `vec3`, etc). Not every node supports the same set of types. Because of the way that dropdowns are implemented as properties with an enum hint, I don't believe it's currently possible to create one main list of `scalar`, `vec2`, `vec3`, `vec4`, and only pick the subset that you want to use for each node.\r\n\r\nIt's not currently idiomatic in the visual shader codebase to share enums between nodes in most cases. However, in this case I think the enums might be fully the same, and can be shared.\r\n\r\n@Chaosus if you don't want to keep working on this, your work on this is still useful, so I can see a second implementation to compare against!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466899191/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466905833","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99033#issuecomment-2466905833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99033","id":2466905833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TCf7p","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followe